<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-NEW SOUTH WALES BEAT FREE STATE 36-11.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-NEW SOUTH WALES BEAT FREE STATE 36-11.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>New South Wales beat Free State 36-11 (halftime 22-11) in a Super 12 match at the Sydney Football Stadium on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>New South Wales - Tries: Alistair Murdoch, Richard Tombs, David Campese, Sam Payne, Michael Brial. Conversions: Matthew Burke (4). Penalty: Matthew Burke.</p>
<p>Free State - Try: Stephen Brink. Penalties: M.J. Smith (2).</p>
